{%- comment -%}
  The category mosaic — one tall tile and four small ones, each a real catalogue
  filter. Port of components/home/category-mosaic.tsx.

  **STILL NOT ON THE HOME PAGE, AND NOW THE BRIEF ASKS FOR IT.** Removed from
  templates/index.json on request 2026-08-20; the website brief's §6 Section 3 is
  "Shop by Category" with example tiles Pants, Tops, Outerwear and New Arrivals.
  The brief is the newer instruction and it wins — this section is what will
  serve it.

  WHAT IS BLOCKING IT is data, not design, and placing it early would break this
  section's own first rule. Every tile has to point at a destination that
  actually matches something, and today neither kind of destination exists:

    - There are no category COLLECTIONS on the store. `/collections/pants` is a
      404 until somebody creates it.
    - `?filter.p.product_type=Pants` does not filter. Shopify's Availability
      facet is the only one defined in Search and Discovery, so a product_type
      parameter is ignored and the page returns the whole catalogue — a link
      that looks like it worked and did not, which is worse than a 404.

  It also needs the taxonomy decision taken first: the eleven design pieces are
  typed by CUT (Wide leg, Culottes, Straight cut) and the 115 Shopee pieces by
  GARMENT (Pants, Vest, Shirt, Bag), so "Pants" today means two different things
  depending on which import a product came from. The direction given is to follow
  the brief and normalise the data — garment in `product_type`, cut moved to
  tags — which is a bulk field update on the store, not an edit here.

  So: the sequence is still hero, new arrivals, Wear Label Custom, customer
  voices, service band, Instagram strip. This section goes back in above the
  voices wall the moment the collections exist, from the theme editor, with no
  edit to this file — it has a preset.

  It is *unplaced*, not forbidden — the distinction this repo draws between this
  section and the made-to-order band, which names a service the studio does not
  offer and must never be placed. Nothing here makes a claim the studio cannot
  keep. That the return costs no code change is one thing the port improved on
  app/page.tsx, where restoring a cut block meant editing the route.

  What must stay true when it does go back: the block order below the voices wall
  exists to keep the wall and the Instagram strip out of one viewport. The
  service band does that job alone today; putting the mosaic back above the
  service band keeps it, putting it below the strip does not.

  This is now a DIVERGENCE from app/page.tsx, which still renders the mosaic.
  The theme is the deliverable and the React app is the reference it was ported
  from, so the two are allowed to drift — but the drift is recorded here and in
  README.md rather than discovered later.

  The label sits on the photograph, so it carries its own surface (a solid chip on
  the small tiles, a heavier weight on the tall one) rather than relying on the
  crop staying dark enough to read against.

  Every destination must be a REAL catalogue query. The design's "Up to 40% off"
  tile is absent because no product on this store carries a compare-at price, and
  the fourth tile is "New in" rather than the design's "Made to order" — that
  filter matches nothing and names a service the studio does not offer.

  The preset's labels are still the CUT vocabulary (Culottes, Straight cut). They
  become the brief's garment vocabulary — Pants, Tops, Outerwear, New Arrivals —
  in the same change that creates the collections, because a label and its
  destination have to move together or the tile lies.

  Photographs fall back from an uploaded image, to the collection's Nth product,
  to the labelled placeholder — so the mosaic needs no art direction of its own to
  stay in step with the catalogue.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign source = collections[section.settings.collection]
  assign feature_image = section.settings.feature_image
  if feature_image == blank and source.products.size > 0
    assign feature_image = source.products.first.featured_image
  endif
-%}

<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter pt-section">
  <nav aria-label="{{ 'home.shop_by_category' | t }}" class="grid gap-7 md:grid-cols-2">
    <a
      href="{{ section.settings.feature_href | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
      class="group relative flex h-112 items-start overflow-hidden rounded-sm"
    >
      {% render 'media', image: feature_image, fill: true, sizes: '(min-width: 768px) 50vw, 100vw', label: 'Category photo', class: 'rounded-none' %}
      <span class="relative flex flex-col gap-2 bg-invert/85 px-8 py-6 text-ink-invert transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) group-hover:bg-invert">
        <span class="text-micro uppercase tracking-label">{{ section.settings.feature_eyebrow }}</span>
        <span class="font-display text-h2 leading-h2">{{ section.settings.feature_label }}</span>
      </span>
    </a>

    <ul class="grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign tile_image = block.settings.image
          if tile_image == blank and source.products.size > forloop.index
            assign tile_image = source.products[forloop.index].featured_image
          endif

          assign even = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2
          if even == 0
            assign chip = 'bg-invert text-ink-invert group-hover:bg-invert-hover'
          else
            assign chip = 'bg-brand text-on-brand group-hover:bg-brand-hover'
          endif
        -%}
        <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <a
            href="{{ block.settings.href | default: routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
            class="group relative flex h-52 items-end justify-end overflow-hidden rounded-sm"
          >
            {% render 'media', image: tile_image, fill: true, sizes: '(min-width: 768px) 25vw, 50vw', label: 'Category photo', class: 'rounded-none' %}
            <span class="relative px-5 py-3.5 text-micro uppercase tracking-label transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) {{ chip }}">
              {{ block.settings.label }}
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </nav>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Category mosaic",
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Every tile must point at a filter that actually matches something. A tile naming a category the catalogue does not carry is a promise the shop cannot keep." },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "collection", "label": "Photograph source" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Feature tile" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "feature_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Shop" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "feature_label", "label": "Label", "default": "Wide leg" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "feature_href", "label": "Link" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "feature_image", "label": "Photograph" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "tile",
      "name": "Tile",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "href", "label": "Link" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Category mosaic",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Culottes" } },
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Straight cut" } },
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "New in" } },
        { "type": "tile", "settings": { "label": "Everything" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
